# Cohort descriptors written by `up --network` — runtime output (live IPs,
# regenerated each deploy; `down --network` deletes them), never committed.
# Everything else in a network directory is its committable identity.
*/nodes/

# Throwaway foundings (see tee/docs/runbook-devnet.md): the whole directory is
# ignored, so a scratch cohort can be founded, torn down, and deleted
# without touching git. A network that matters gets an unprefixed
# directory — its identity is committed.
tmp-*/
